ABSTRACT: As satellite networks are deployed more widely and used in a greater variety of ways, security issues have increasingly become a focal point of concern for the international community. Penetration testing is a proactive security assessment technology that involves simulating intrusions using attack tools and identifying existing security vulnerabilities in the target networks. This paper systematically analyzes the characteristics and laws of attack behaviors against satellite networks based on an overview of the composition of satellite networks, with a focus on elaborating the application of penetration testing technologies in the satellite field. According to the penetration decision-making mechanism, it categorizes the relevant technologies into rule-based penetration testing and model-based penetration testing, detailing the specific applications of these two types of technologies in satellite network environments. Finally, integrating the latest advancements in large language model technology for penetration testing, it forecasts the future development trends of satellite network penetration testing technologies. © (2026), (Journal of Computer Engineering and Applications Beijing Co., Ltd.; Science Press). All rights reserved.

